.TH mbeditviz-qt 1 "8 November 2026" "MB-System 5.0" "MB-System 5.0"
.SH NAME
\fBmbeditviz-qt\fP \- Bathymetry editor and patch test tool (Qt6 version).

.SH VERSION
Version 5.0

.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBmbeditviz-qt\fP
.br
[--delete-input-file {-R}
.br
--format=format_id {-Fformat_id}
.br
--help {-H}
.br
--input=file {-Ifile}
.br
--simple-mean-grid {-G}
.br
--verbose {-V}]

.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBmbeditviz-qt\fP is a Qt6 port of \fBmbeditviz\fP. It lists swath files,
grids the soundings of the files to be edited and shows the grid in a map.
Soundings picked in the map with an area, a region or a navigation track open
in a 3D soundings view, where they can be flagged and unflagged and where
roll, pitch and heading biases, a time lag and a Snell correction can be
tested and optimised. The edits are written to edit save files, which
\fBmbprocess\fP applies.

The two programs share their program logic, the gridding and editing code and
the \fBmbview\fP drawing code, so they read the same swath files and datalists
and write the same edit save files and parameter files; a file edited with one
program can be edited further with the other. Two programs cannot edit one
file at the same time. The map is drawn by the original OpenGL drawing code of
\fBmbview\fP in an OpenGL 2.1 compatibility context; the map window is
described in \fBmbgrdviz\fP(1). The windows can be resized.

